# Board-specific knobs for the Slint software renderer.
#
# Keeping these in Kconfig rather than in CMakeLists.txt means a new board needs
# nothing but a boards/<board>.conf file. The Rust target is derived from the
# CPU that Zephyr already knows about, and the peripherals are discovered from
# the devicetree, so there is no board list to extend.

config SLINT_ZEPHYR_RGB565_NATIVE_ENDIAN
	bool "The display driver takes RGB565 in native endian"
	help
	  Zephyr's PIXEL_FORMAT_RGB_565 is big endian. Some drivers declare that
	  format but consume native endian data. Set this to skip the byte swap.

config SLINT_ZEPHYR_SCALE_FACTOR
	string "Logical pixel to physical pixel ratio"
	default "1"
	help
	  Everything in the .slint file is written in logical pixels. This is how
	  many physical pixels one of them covers. A 320x240 panel wants 1, and a
	  bigger panel or a desktop window wants 2 so that the same layout stays
	  readable. The software renderer bakes glyphs at build time, so this is a
	  build-time setting rather than a runtime one.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
